starts on Android \n\u25c6 Expo UI is stable \n\u25c6 iOS widgets are stable \n\u25c6 expo-router rebuilt from scratch \n\u25c6 Inline native modules \n\u25c6 Brownfield multi-app support\n\nThe obvious themes are speed and stability. But there are a lot of other interesting changes (like Expo Router decoupling itself form React Navigation). Get all the nuance and detail in the changelog below \u2193","url":"https://x.com/expo/status/2052470611117834611","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/we-just-cut-the-sdk-56-beta-50-faster-ios-builds-precompiled-xcframeworks-40-faster-cold-yw1jf2cke","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--0_ODbtD2--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2008","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-07T20:20:43.171Z"},{"id":"uImC74w6P","title":"Android builds on EAS are now ~50% faster.\n\nGradle caching stores task outputs and reuses them between builds. Especially helpful for projects with many native modules.\n\nEnable with \ud835\ude74\ud835\ude70\ud835\ude82_\ud835\ude76\ud835\ude81\ud835\ude70\ud835\ude73\ud835\ude7b\ud835\ude74_\ud835\ude72\ud835\ude70\ud835\ude72\ud835\ude77\ud835\ude74=\ud835\udff7.\n\nLink to the changelog \u2193","url":"https://x.com/expo/status/2049885240685199799","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/android-builds-on-eas-are-now-50-faster-gradle-caching-stores-task-outputs-and-reuses-them-betwe-uimc74w6p","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--qPvKM23u--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2009","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-01T05:06:44.110Z"},{"id":"2rnRDZipm","title":"Update: Expo Go iOS SDK 55 is in App Store review.  \n\nThe current TestFlight build expires Wed April 22. If the review isn't complete by the 22nd you can build your own with `eas go` OR you can run Expo Go in a simulator.  \n\nExpo Go for SDK 54 is unaffected.","url":"https://x.com/expo/status/2046330705408602314","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/update-expo-go-ios-sdk-55-is-in-app-store-review-the-current-testflight-build-expires-wed-april-2rnrdzipm","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--ZrL_HSsR--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2006","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-20T21:26:05.490Z"},{"id":"JGUpjZQLg","title":"\ud83d\ude4c Expo is the best it's ever been, and it's about to get a lot better.\n\nWe raised a Series B so we can go faster on the things that matter to you: faster builds, smoother native integrations, and the services to make end-to-end app development a delightful experience.\n\nThere is a lot of work to do. This round led by @Georgian_io puts us in position to go do it!","url":"https://x.com/expo/status/2044787761589432821","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/expo-is-the-best-it-s-ever-been-and-it-s-about-to-get-a-lot-better-we-raised-a-series-b-so-we-c-jgupjzqlg","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--1KxV4ohY--/f_auto/v1722860400/public/Placeholder%2007","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-16T16:18:42.471Z"},{"id":"SJlQMTFrP","title":"\ud83e\udd29 Just pulled the first cohort of beta users off the waitlist....\n\nIf you are super passionate about getting into this beta and working with Expo Agent let us know. \n\nWe want to prioritize people that we can anticipate getting meaningful feedback from.","url":"https://x.com/expo/status/2032561491346616535","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/just-pulled-the-first-cohort-of-beta-users-off-the-waitlist-if-you-are-super-passionate-about-sjlqmtfrp","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--foaA6JGU--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2004","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-13T21:14:51.125Z"},{"id":"3pUcNHiRr","title":"\ud83e\udd2f Expo Router v55 is a big one.\n\n\u2662 Stack API for native headers\n\u2662 Native Tabs + Material 3 dynamic colors\n\u2662 iOS toolbars + zoom transitions\n\u2662 expo-server, headers, experimental SSR + loaders\n\u2662 Split view on iPad (beta)\n\nFull blog with instructions and demos \u2193 https://t.co/fzu2g4MXxh","url":"https://x.com/expo/status/2028508262371623323","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/expo-router-v55-is-a-big-one-stack-api-for-native-headers-native-tabs-material-3-dynamic-c-3pucnhirr","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--ZrL_HSsR--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2006","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-02T18:14:29.125Z"},{"id":"bZOqKYkne","title":"Expo SDK 55 is here\ud83d\ude05\n\nReact Native 0.83. React 19.2. Legacy Architecture dropped. New Architecture is the default.\n\n\u25c6 75% smaller update downloads with Hermes bytecode diffing \n\u25c6 Expo Router v7 \ud83e\udd2f\n\u25c6 Brownfield isolation via expo-brownfield \n\u25c6 AI tooling: MCP + agent skills for Claude Code\n\u25c6 Expo UI much improved for both Swift and Jetpack Compose\n\nThere is so much more...it feels futile to try and isolate a few bullets...check out the full release notes and let us know what you think \u2193","url":"https://x.com/expo/status/2026811977990025364","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/expo-sdk-55-is-here-react-native-0-83-react-19-2-legacy-architecture-dropped-new-architecture-i-bzoqkykne","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--P4t4XyoV--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2001","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-26T04:53:12.850Z"},{"id":"b7X5P5FrM","title":"Security notice: incorrect plugin configuration guidance in SDK 50 migration documentation may expose a sensitive key","url":"https://blog.expo.dev/security-notice-incorrect-plugin-configuration-guidance-in-sdk-50-migration-documentation-may-6464aab65704","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/security-notice-incorrect-plugin-configuration-guidance-in-sdk-50-migration-documentation-may-expos-b7x5p5frm","summary":"The migration guide from sentry-expo to @sentry/react-native provided incorrect plugin configuration guidance in SDK 50, exposing a sensitive key in the app. Sensitive values should be kept on a server and accessed through secure APIs. Check if your app is affected by reviewing the given configuration examples.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7396463b9ed58295793a917ac434b93f?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-02-27T03:03:05.128Z"},{"id":"F6DxHWXuP","title":"Expo Router v3","url":"https://blog.expo.dev/expo-router-v3-4f12ffee409b","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/expo-router-v3-f6dxhwxup","summary":"Expo Router v3 has been released with support for API Routes (beta), bundle splitting for web, 2x faster web builds, and more highly requested features!","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/3949b782f84e046c64505b317e7a9a45?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":30,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-01-23T16:56:13.166Z"},{"id":"S3vxiEpdW","title":"Webpack support in Expo CLI is now deprecated","url":"https://blog.expo.dev/webpack-support-in-expo-cli-is-now-deprecated-e9831d7eb631","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/webpack-support-in-expo-cli-is-now-deprecated-s3vxiepdw","summary":"Expo CLI no longer supports Webpack for bundling websites. Instead, Expo recommends using Metro bundler and Expo Router for building websites. Metro bundler has many advantages, including incremental bundling, aggressive caching, and a multi-dimensional graph for bundling multiple different platforms simultaneously. Expo has added several web-specific features to Metro, such as file-based routing, CSS, Sass, PostCSS, Tailwind, fast refresh, static rendering, API routes, and more. Third party integrations like Storybook and Next.js still support Metro bundler. Users with custom features can refer to Expo's documentation to implement those features using universal Metro bundler.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/4de3cdbdb6904004e9ab7e1ea0308b51?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-01-18T19:50:22.449Z"}],"top_posts":[{"id":"F6DxHWXuP","title":"Expo Router v3","url":"https://blog.expo.dev/expo-router-v3-4f12ffee409b","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/expo-router-v3-f6dxhwxup","summary":"Expo Router v3 has been released with support for API Routes (beta), bundle splitting for web, 2x faster web builds, and more highly requested features!","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/3949b782f84e046c64505b317e7a9a45?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":30,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-01-23T16:56:13.166Z"},{"id":"RSqTcSkH8","title":"Announcing Expo Router v1","url":"https://blog.expo.dev/announcing-expo-router-v1-1d97d7833605?source=rss----d397bd202faa---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/announcing-expo-router-v1-rsqtcskh8","summary":"Announcing Expo Router v1. The First File-Based Router for Native. Learn more about what's possible in Expo Router in the v1 RC announcement and in the Expo Router documentation. Help us out by starring Expo on GitHub, filing bug reports in issues or opening discussions with questions or proposals.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/00141edd4e7d0a494a51278f5564d59c","num_upvotes":20,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2023-02-22T21:01:27.369Z"},{"id":"XKCn6536b","title":"The New Expo CLI","url":"https://blog.expo.dev/the-new-expo-cli-f4250d8e3421?source=rss----d397bd202faa---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-new-expo-cli-xkcn6536b","summary":"The new tooling has incredible tests, covering nearly aspect of the tooling. In early 2021 (Expo SDK 41), we introduced support for custom native code in managed workflow projects with EAS Build and a command called expo prebuild. We\u2019ve already begun shipping new Metro features starting with experimental web support, and have PRs open for context modules.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1933e8064efbedfcb10c5dd60bfc25a2","num_upvotes":19,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2022-08-11T17:04:21.721Z"},{"id":"XUp49WlWZ","title":"Xcode 15 and iOS 17","url":"https://blog.expo.dev/xcode-15-and-ios-17-eb87099c0078?source=rss----d397bd202faa---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/xcode-15-and-ios-17-xup49wlwz","summary":"Xcode 15 and iOS 17 have been released with improvements to support these new versions.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/5a596808572f4573667a0e1a75abf39c?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":11,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2023-09-29T22:55:00.594Z"},{"id":"aERyvWxY6","title":"Expo Router v3 beta is now available","url":"https://blog.expo.dev/expo-router-v3-beta-is-now-available-eab52baf1e3e?source=rss----d397bd202faa---4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/expo-router-v3-beta-is-now-available-aeryvwxy6","summary":"Expo Router v3 beta is now available, offering new features such as faster static website exports, smaller base bundle size, API Routes, and bundle splitting. Users can upgrade their projects from Expo Router v2 to v3 and should be aware of the breaking changes. Beta testers are encouraged to report issues on GitHub.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/2befbffbe42a3f570f75c4bb29229dc0?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":16,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-12-12T21:04:44.958Z"}],"similar_handles":["srestories","cortex","devrelx","risingstack","theserverlessedge"],"opposite_handles":["dailydevworld","on_leuwcq","horde","watercooler","dotnetsquad"],"similar":[{"id":"srestories","handle":"srestories","name":"SRE Stories","is_squad":false,"x":-1.1067,"y":-0.0934,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":22,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/f59b6840d1bb40f38a64932d7bb21e